    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32294" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκύπτω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>peep out of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰγείρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					50.13
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τῶν οἴκων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ant.Lib.
					39.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκύψασαν ἁλῶναι</span> to be
			caught <i>peeping out</i> (Reiske for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκ-</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				790
			</span></i>: generally, <i>pop out,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				1052
			</span></i> ; of a snail's eyes, Teucer ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				10.455e
			</span></i> : metaph., <i>proceed forth,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ νοητοῦ εἰς οὐρανόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
					4.3.15
				</span></i>
			; cf.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκέκυφεν: ἀνωρθώθη</span>
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ωσεν</span> cod.), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans., <i>put forth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				15.21
			</span></i>.</div>
